-- statement:
--   The integer weight `w = aT gT cT` against `2^{3P-σ} (2α)⁻¹ e_j`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6AMath1`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6A.weight_err (P σ s t α H k : ℕ) (ht : 0 < t) (hst : s ≤ t) (hα : 2 ≤ α) (hH : 1 ≤ H)
--       (hP : 2 ≤ P) (hσP : σ ≤ 2 * P)
--       (hσ : Real.exp (Real.pi * (s * (t - s) * H ^ 2 : ℕ) / ((t ^ 2 * α ^ 2 : ℕ) : ℝ)) ≤ 2 ^ σ) (j : ℤ) :
--       |((aT P s t α H k j * gT P s t α H k j * cT P σ s t α H k : ℤ) : ℝ) -
--         2 ^ (3 * P) * (2 ^ σ)⁻¹ * ((2 * α : ℝ)⁻¹ * ew s t α k j)| ≤ 6 * 2 ^ (2 * P)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** A lines (PR #5 block chirp), part 1: the block-chirp `S'` map and its error
--
--   The output axis (length `t`) is cut into blocks of `B = 2H` consecutive indices. For an output `k`
--   the block centre is `k_c = ⌊k/B⌋ B + H`, the offset `κ = k - k_c ∈ [-H, H)`, and the input centre
--   is `j_c = round(s k_c / t)`. With `A = t j - s k_c` the exponent of the Gaussian weight splits as
--
--   `(j - s k/t)² = ((t-s) A² + s (A - t κ)²) / t³ - s (t-s) κ² / t²`   (`expo_split`)
--
--   so `e^{-π(j - sk/t)²/α²} = a · g · C` with an input scaling `a` (per block), a correlation kernel
--   `g` (per block, a function of `j - κ`), and an output scaling `C = e^{π s(t-s)κ²/(t²α²)}` that is the
--   same for every block (`ew_split`). The machine computes, for every output,
--
--   `chirpA U k = (Σ_{|j - j_c| < W} aT_j gT_{j-κ} U_{j mod s}) · cT_κ  tdiv  2^{3P-σ}`
--
--   with `aT ≈ 2^P a`, `gT ≈ 2^P g` (`expNeg`) and `cT ≈ 2^{P-σ} C / (2α)` (`expPos`, `betaT`).
--
--   **`chirpA_err`**: for every input in the disc and every `k`,
--   `‖chirpA U k - 2^p S'(U/2^p)_k‖ ≤ 12 W 2^{p+σ} / 2^P + 2`, as soon as the window contains the
--   `Sapprox` window (`H + m + 3 ≤ W`) and `e^{π s(t-s)H²/(t²α²)} ≤ 2^σ`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
